 "about": "Peoples: the range a culture's strangers are drawn from (KCHAR.stranger, src/10-rig.js). ancestry: each MakeHuman race share drawn from [lo, hi] (then normalised). skin: colour stops, light to dark; a stranger's tone falls anywhere along them. hair and eyes: the colours drawn from; grey: the age slider value above which hair greys. beard: odds a man wears one. morph: a slider drawn from [lo, hi] instead of the default spread. styles: hair ids drawn first (three times in four) per body. Sources: LORE.md section 6 and 7, and the owner's notes (Chichani: ashen-brown skin, dark hair; Beast Riders: vaguely Asiatic or Amerindian, blond to brown hair). Chichani eyes run to amber and red (night vision, after the Dunmer); a proposal. The rest are proposals from each culture's real-world references; change them freely. outfits: per body, per tier, the clothes (torso, legs, feet) a people's strangers wear, and the body mods a tier has (mods: a temple guard's second pair of arms); mods (of a people): the mods all its strangers have (the Hykkousoi's rib gills, tools/mods.py); a four-armed tier wears a four-armed top (KCHAR.fits); tiers: [tier, share] in draw order (KCHAR.stranger). style_share: the share of strangers whose hair is one of its styles (0.75 when absent; 1: only its styles).",
